course: dictionary
lesson: 13617
title: Signs and hints
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An indication is a sign that shows something is true or will happen. It can also be a hint, a small clue that tells you something without saying it outright. «Dark clouds are an indication of rain.» The clouds are a sign, so rain is probably coming.
explain: «She gave no indication that she was upset.» She did not say she was upset, and she did not show it, so there was no hint at all. Ask yourself: is this a sign or a hint? If it is, indication probably fits.
explain: Scientists use the word too. A measuring tool, like a thermometer, gives a reading, and that reading is an indication of how hot something is. «A colour change is an indication of a reaction» means the change tells you something is happening.
explain: You will often see the phrases «an indication of», «give an indication» and «there is every indication that». The last one means there are strong signs that something is true.
fact: Indication is a noun. One indication, many indications.
fact: «Indication» means a sign that shows something is true or will happen.
fact: «Indication» also means a suggestion or hint.
fact: On a measuring instrument, an indication is the reading you see, such as the number on a thermometer.
fact: «There is every indication that» means there are strong signs that something is true.
exercise: «Dark clouds are an indication of rain.» What does indication mean in this sentence? | A bright rainbow | A toy umbrella | *A sign that rain is coming | A loud clap of thunder
exercise: «She gave no indication that she was upset.» Did she give any hint that she was upset? | Yes, she shouted at everyone | Yes, she cried loudly | *No, there was no hint at all | Yes, she was smiling
exercise: A thermometer shows the number 30. What is that number? | A sweet drink | *An indication of how hot it is | A pet name for the thermometer | A kind of ruler
test: «There is every indication that the bus will be late.» What does this mean? | The bus has no driver | The bus is painted red | *There are strong signs the bus will be late | The bus is definitely early
test: Which word is a good synonym for indication? | *Sign | Cupboard | Mountain | Music
exam: «The green light is an indication that the door is open.» What does indication mean here? | A guess with no reason at all | A green paint on the door | A lovely smell from the room | *A sign that shows the door is open
